      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "stem": "Which statement accurately describes the relationship between programming skill and AR software categories?",
      "correct": "Standalone authoring tools require the least programming skill, while low-level libraries require the highest skill.",
      "wrong": [
        "Low-level frameworks are generally easier to use than standalone authoring tools.",
        "Most rapid prototyping tools fall into the category requiring the least programming skill.",
        "All categories of AR software require similar levels of advanced coding proficiency."
      ],
      "explanation_correct": "Standalone tools are designed for ease of use, minimizing coding requirements, while low-level libraries provide deep functionality that demands advanced programming.",
      "explanations_wrong": [
        "Low-level frameworks are generally easier to use than standalone authoring tools. (Low-level libraries are inherently complex and require significant programming expertise.)",
        "Most rapid prototyping tools fall into the category requiring the least programming skill. (Rapid prototyping sits in the middle of the skill spectrum, not at the extreme of least skill.)",
        "All categories of AR software require similar levels of advanced coding proficiency. (The fundamental point of the categorization is that the skill requirement varies widely.)"
