      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "stem": "In an experiment testing system usability, what does a dependent variable represent?",
      "correct": "The outcome or result that is expected to change based on the factors tested.",
      "wrong": [
        "The feature or factor that the experimenter controls and changes.",
        "A general measurement that is used to describe the user base demographics.",
        "The pre-existing condition of the system before the evaluation begins."
      ],
      "explanation_correct": "A dependent variable is the data that is observed and depends on changes made to the factors being studied.",
      "explanations_wrong": [
        "This describes the independent variable, which is the factor the experimenter manipulates.",
        "This describes a confounding variable or demographic data, which is not the primary dependent variable.",
        "This describes a baseline condition, which is not the outcome measure itself."
      ]
