  ],
  "recap": "Empirical evaluation is a research method that involves observing real users in a real-world setting after a system has been fully built. The initial step in this research process is defining testable questions, which allows for objective data collection. To design these experiments, it is essential to differentiate between independent variables (the factors being tested) and dependent variables (the results that are measured)."
